# Schemas and Enums

## Schema folder

One folder per entity method, named in PascalCase: `Schema/Get/`, `Schema/ChangeSituation/`, `Schema/FindFinalCustomer/`.

### Files for an operation

| File | Extends | Role |
|------|---------|------|
| `GetParams.php` | `QueryParams` | Query filters |
| `GetResponse.php` | `BaseResponseRootObject` | Root payload (`data`) |
| `GetResponseData.php` | `BaseResponseObject` | One element of `data` |
| `GetResponseDataEstoque.php` | `BaseResponseObject` | Nested object under `estoque` |

Reference: `src/Entities/Contatos/Schema/`, `src/Entities/CamposCustomizados/Schema/`, `src/Entities/Produtos/Schema/`.

### Params class

`readonly final class GetParams extends QueryParams`.

- Constructor parameters are the Bling query fields, with defaults of `null`.
- A backed enum is accepted as `EnumType|scalar|null` and stored as `$enum->value`.
- A `\DateTimeInterface|string|null` argument is passed through `prepareStringOrDateParam`. The second argument is `true` when Bling expects a datetime (`Contatos\Schema\Get\GetParams`).
- The constructor finishes with `parent::__construct(objectToArray($this))`.
- The entity method accepts `GetParams|array|null $params = null` and passes `$params` as `queryParams`.

### Response root

`readonly final class GetResponse extends BaseResponseRootObject`.

List payloads type `data` as an array and register the item in `fromRules`:

```php
protected static function fromRules(): array
{
    return ['data' => GetResponseData::class];
}
```

`fromResponse` rejects a null body with `throwForInconsistentResponseOptions`, then `return self::from($response->body->content)`.

An empty success (`DeleteResponse`, `Contatos\Schema\Update\UpdateResponse`) implements `fromResponse(...): null`, rejects a non-null body, and returns `null`.

A header the caller must keep is merged in `fromResponse` before `from`. `Homologacao\Schema\Get\GetResponse` sets `'hash' => $response->headers->content['x-bling-homologacao']`.

### Nested objects and lists

Name the class `<Parent><FieldInPascalCase>`: `FindResponseData` → `FindResponseDataEndereco` → `FindResponseDataEnderecoDados`.

A property typed as a single schema class is parsed by `BaseResponseObject::from` with no `fromRules` entry. A property typed as an array of schema objects has a `fromRules` entry (`FindResponseData::$tiposContato`).

### Discriminated unions

One `readonly final` class per variant, suffix `DTO`, living in `Schema/@shared/` when several operations share it. `from` throws `BlingParseResponsePayloadException` when the discriminator does not match, then calls `parent::from`. The property on the parent is the union (`Unica|Parcelada|Normal|Semanal|null $ocorrencia` in `ContasPagar\Schema\Find\FindResponseData`).

## Enums

`Enum/<Name>.php` is a backed enum. The backing type is `string` or `int`, matching the JSON value. The docblock is `Enumerador de ...`.

```php
enum Situacao: string
{
    case ATIVO = 'A';
    case INATIVO = 'I';
}
```

Put the enum in `src/Entities/@shared/Enum/` only when at least two modules share those cases (`UF`, `TipoPessoa`, `Genero`). Resource-specific `Situacao` enums stay next to the entity.

## Rules

- One operation per `Schema/<Operation>/` folder.
- Schema classes contain data and `from` / `fromResponse` / `fromRules` only.
- Property names match the Bling JSON keys.
- A `{ "id": int }` object uses `Entities\Shared\DTO\Schema\Id`.
